$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM To a 5 mL round bottomed flask equipped with a magnetic stirrer bar and
reflux condenser is added MIDA-vinyl silane 1, Pd(OAc)2 (5 mol%) SPhos
(10 mol%) and aryl halide (1.2 equiv.) and the mixture purged with argon
for 5 min after which dioxane (0.08M) was added and the solution stirred
for a further 10 min. K3PO4 solution (7.5 equiv., 3M solution degassed)
was then added and the mixture stirred at 60 °C until TLC analysis showed
complete consumption of starting material (TLC eluted with EtOAc). The
mixture was diluted with DCM and passed through a pad of Celite, washing
with DCM and EtOAc and the solution concentrated.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, Suzuki coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM MIDA-Vinylsilanes: Selective Cross-Couplings and Applications to the
Synthesis of Functionalized Stilbenes
